   "q": {
    "en": "A stone is dropped from a height of 45 m. The time it takes to reach the ground is ($g = 10$ m s⁻²):"
   },
   "options": [
    {
     "en": "4.5 s"
    },
    {
     "en": "9 s"
    },
    {
     "en": "2 s"
    },
    {
     "en": "3 s"
    }
   ],
   "answer": 3,
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "Dropped means it starts from rest: $u = 0$."
    },
    {
     "en": "$h = \\frac12 g t^2$, so $t = \\sqrt{2h/g}$"
    },
    {
     "en": "$t = \\sqrt{90/10} = \\sqrt{9} = 3$ s"
    },
    {
     "en": "Trap: 4.5 s comes from $h/g$ without the square root."
    }
   ],
   "idealTime": 45,
   "difficulty": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "phy11-1-02-002",
   "chapter": {
